  "worked_solution": "We must have $x=0$ at the $y$-intercepts. \n\nSo, we need to substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the circle and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-3)^{2}+(y-1)^{2} & =16 \\\\ (0-3)^{2}+(y-1)^{2} & =16 \\\\ 9+(y-1)^{2} & =16 \\\\ (y-1)^{2} & =7 \\\\ y-1 & =\\pm \\sqrt{7} \\\\ y & =1\\pm \\sqrt{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercepts occur at the points $(0,1-\\sqrt{7})$ and $(0,1+\\sqrt{7}).$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
